---
title: "PDF Export - Customising Content"
enterprise: true
---

PDF export uses value getters and value formatters, but does not export cell-renderer output. Export callbacks can replace the resulting text without changing the grid.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
api.exportDataAsPdf({
    processCellCallback: (params) => params.formatValue(params.value),
    processHeaderCallback: (params) => params.column.getDisplayName(),
    processGroupHeaderCallback: (params) => params.columnGroup.getDisplayName(),
    processRowGroupCallback: (params) => `Group: ${params.node.key ?? ''}`,
});
```

The following shared export options are supported:

- `processCellCallback` customises body cell values.
- `processHeaderCallback` customises column header values.
- `processGroupHeaderCallback` customises column-group header values.
- `processRowGroupCallback` customises row-group values. PDF indentation is applied independently of the returned text.
- `shouldRowBeSkipped` excludes individual rows.

